\begin{lemma}[Dimension three gives corank one]\label{lem:corank}
For an elliptic curve with full rational two-torsion,
$\dim_{\F_2}\Sel_2=3$ implies $\operatorname{corank}_{\Z_2}\Sel_{2^\infty}=1$.
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
The finite Kummer sequence gives $r+\dim\Sha[2]=1$.
Write $\Sha[2^\infty]=(\Q_2/\Z_2)^t\oplus F$ with $F$ finite.
The Cassels--Tate pairing on the quotient by the maximal divisible
subgroup is nondegenerate and alternating for an elliptic curve
\cite{poonenstoll}. Its finite primary cyclic factors are paired,
so $\dim F[2]$ is even. Thus $F=0$ and $r+t=1$. The restriction of
the pairing to $F[2]$ need not be nondegenerate and is not used.
\end{proof}

\begin{proposition}[Fixed-field polynomial count]\label{prop:v5-artin-patterns}
There is a function $\omega(N)\to0$, depending on the fixed data, such that
whenever $\omega(N)\sqrt N\leq T=o(\sqrt N)$,
\begin{equation}\label{eq:v5-artin-patterns}
 \sum_{u\leq N}\sum_{1\leq w\leq T}
       \prod_{j=1}^k\Lambda'_j(u+c_jw^2)
       =\mathfrak S\,NT+o(NT),
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}\label{eq:v5-artin-series}
 \mathfrak S=
 \left(\frac D{\varphi(D)}\right)^k
 \mathbb E_{u,w\bmod D}\prod_j\mu_j(u+c_jw^2)
 \prod_{p\nmid D}\beta_p,
 \quad
 \beta_p=\mathbb E_{u,w\bmod p}
       \prod_j\frac p{p-1}1_{p\nmid u+c_jw^2}.
\end{equation}
The same statement on $N/2\leq u\leq N$ has main term
$\mathfrak SNT/2$.
\end{proposition}
\begin{proof}
We specify how the linear Artin theorem and the published polynomial
transference results combine. Frei--Tinkov\'a~\cite{v5ft}, Theorem~1.4,
applies to any fixed finite-complexity system of affine-linear forms,
with bounded linear coefficients and bounded constant coefficients divided
by the ambient scale, uniformly over convex regions in a fixed box.
Its conductor factor is precisely \eqref{eq:v5-mu}; a finite union of
conjugacy classes follows by addition. This is their unconditional theorem,
not their primitive-root theorem, Theorem~1.2.
